# Real-time Messaging Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines apply to all real-time chat and messaging components. While specific implementations may vary based on messaging protocol (WebSockets, MQTT, etc.), the core principles remain consistent.

## Best Practices
- Implement proper connection state management
- Design for message delivery state tracking (sending, sent, delivered, read)
- Handle reconnection logic with exponential backoff
- Support offline message queueing and sync
- Implement proper message ordering with timestamps
- Use separate channels for different conversation types
- Handle concurrent message edits and deletes
- Implement typing indicators with debouncing
- Support incremental message history loading

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Organize real-time components by responsibility:
  ```
  lib/
    data/
      datasources/
        remote/
          messaging_socket_service.dart
          messaging_api_service.dart
        local/
          message_cache_service.dart
    domain/
      entities/
        message.dart
        conversation.dart
      repositories/
        message_repository.dart
      usecases/
        send_message_usecase.dart
        receive_message_usecase.dart
    presentation/
      blocs/
        messaging/
          messaging_bloc.dart
          messaging_event.dart
          messaging_state.dart
      screens/
        chat_screen.dart
      widgets/
        message_list.dart
        message_input.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use enum for message states: `MessageStatus.sent`, `MessageStatus.delivered`
- Format timestamps consistently using UTC
- Implement proper pagination for message history
- Use optimistic UI updates for message sending
- Handle multipart messages properly
- Use consistent message metadata schema
- Name WebSocket events descriptively: `message_received`, `message_read`

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Implement message batching for bulk operations
- Use pagination for message history loading
- Optimize images and media before transmission
- Implement efficient local caching strategy
- Use compression for large messages or media
- Prioritize UI responsiveness over background operations
- Implement proper connection pooling
- Use efficient serialization formats
- Consider binary protocols for high-throughput systems

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test connection state transitions thoroughly
- Simulate poor network conditions
- Verify message ordering under various conditions
- Test concurrent message operations
- Validate offline functionality
- Test reconnection logic with various failure modes
- Verify proper cleanup of socket resources
- Test memory usage with large message histories
- Implement load testing for high-volume scenarios
